secureshellgo (1.4.2~noble1) noble; urgency=medium

  * Credential storage keeps one rule instead of a menu: the system keyring
    when it answers, otherwise an encrypted file in the app's own data
    directory, chosen automatically and without asking. Vaults written by
    1.4.1 still open. Device encryption no longer runs the password-stretching
    key derivation over a random key, which removes a pause of roughly a
    second from the first save and from every start on machines with no
    keyring.
  * A server with the sftp subsystem disabled no longer leaves the file
    browser spinning for ever. The subsystem is confirmed before the panel
    waits on it, so a refusal is reported instead of hanging.
  * Disconnecting the last session returns to the host list immediately
    rather than showing an empty window until the connection has finished
    closing.
  * The host actions menu and the copy-to-server picker scroll when they are
    taller than the window instead of overflowing and hiding their last
    entries.
  * A snap install is told the interface command that grants keyring access
    again, rather than being told its keyring is locked.

 -- Dhiva Labs <dhivakar1010@gmail.com>  Tue, 04 Aug 2026 03:40:00 +0530

